# Global attributes. Git uses this path by default as core.attributesFile, so
# nothing has to point at it. A repository's own .gitattributes always wins over
# anything here, so these are defaults for repos that have not bothered.

# --- Line endings ------------------------------------------------------------
# core.autocrlf=input normalises to LF on commit, which is right for everything
# except the file types Windows insists on reading as CRLF. cmd.exe will
# misparse a .bat with LF endings, and PowerShell's parser is unreliable on
# here-strings with LF, so these three are pinned regardless of platform.
*.bat	text eol=crlf
*.cmd	text eol=crlf
*.ps1	text eol=crlf

# Deliberately NOT here: a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`. Globally that changes
# how every repo without its own .gitattributes normalises, which turns into a
# whole-tree diff the first time you touch an existing checkout. It belongs in
# a repository's .gitattributes, where collaborators can see it.

# --- Diff hunk headers -------------------------------------------------------
# These name git's built-in funcname patterns, so `@@` hunk headers show the
# enclosing function or heading instead of a random nearby line. Only drivers
# confirmed present in this git are listed; an unknown name is silently ignored
# rather than an error, which makes typos here invisible.
*.md	diff=markdown
*.Rmd	diff=markdown
*.qmd	diff=markdown
*.py	diff=python
*.sh	diff=bash
*.bash	diff=bash
